    "description": "OrderProjection subscribes to an order-events topic and updates a reporting database. OrderEventProcessor is deployed continuously but may be scaled to zero during a nightly maintenance window while orders continue to be published. The broker supports stable consumer-group identities, retained events for seven days, and committed delivery positions. The deployment configuration must use a fixed group identifier so OrderEventProcessor resumes from its last committed position after a restart rather than creating a fresh subscription that misses the outage. Processing is at least once, so duplicate OrderApproved and OrderRefunded events may arrive; the database update must be idempotent. Events older than the retention window are a recovery incident and must raise an operational alert. The team must choose whether downtime should preserve a replayable backlog or whether the projection may intentionally remain incomplete and be rebuilt separately.",
    "decision_statement": "Should OrderProjection retain a stable subscription identity and committed broker position so events published during downtime are replayed after it returns?",
    "notes": "durable-subscriber fits the stable group identity with committed positions replaying the downtime backlog; event-driven-consumer and polling-consumer are the delivery-style alternatives, with message-endpoint supporting the endpoint wiring."
  },
